    "notes": "Parameter/capture modes and type ownership qualifiers are explicit, closed, and separate identity axes. An ordinary `mut name: T` parameter acquires its argument once and commits a callee-owned mutable local with no caller alias/writeback; `name: mut T` is instead an ordinary channel carrying a unique mutable owner. Function types preserve the published `(borrow T) -> R` family by committing a direct item-leading ParameterMode only after the same ParenTypeSyntax owner observes `->`; `((mut T)) -> R` preserves a qualified input on an ordinary channel. Type qualifiers normalize exactly to UNQUALIFIED/OWNED/BORROWED/MUT/INOUT, allow no stacking or implicit variance, retain exact HIR/API residue, require region binding for BORROWED/INOUT, and lower by one closed MIR table. Unbound escape selects BORROW_ESCAPE_OWNER_REGION; other illegal qualifier composition/context selects OWNERSHIP_MODE_ADMISSION_FAILED. Product execution remains NOT_RUN.",
